WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:03.330
Run kube-noob next to your
own app, in the same pod.

2
00:00:07.450 --> 00:00:12.165
It listens only on localhost, so only
the containers in that pod can call it.

3
00:00:15.450 --> 00:00:20.181
It makes no outbound calls, so its
network policy allows DNS only.

4
00:00:20.181 --> 00:00:24.410
kube-noob gets no Service, no
Route and no token to manage.

5
00:00:25.617 --> 00:00:29.310
On a test cluster that enforces
Pod Security restricted,

6
00:00:29.310 --> 00:00:34.257
the app asks it to audit a Deployment
and diagnose a crash, over localhost.

7
00:00:37.617 --> 00:00:41.884
In our test cluster it peaked at
94 mebibytes, well under its limit.

8
00:00:44.617 --> 00:00:49.174
One example manifest, audited
for OpenShift 4.20 and later.

9
00:00:49.174 --> 00:00:51.337
Get it at kube-noob dot com.
